<description>
Complete each framed motif by reflecting it to the opposite side of its frame.

Input structure
- A background canvas contains one or more large same-color rectangular frame
  objects and a smaller motif color inside each frame's bounding box.

Rule
- Infer the frame color as the unique non-background color with the largest
  area; the other non-background color is the motif color.
- For each frame bounding box, reflect all motif pixels inside that box:
  wide frames mirror left-to-right, while tall frames mirror top-to-bottom.

Key insight
- The frame's aspect ratio identifies the symmetry direction, and the output is
  the union of the original motif with its reflection inside the same frame.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "summary": "Complete each framed motif by reflecting it to the opposite side of its rectangular frame.",
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "motif-color pixels inside each large frame-color object bbox",
  "transform": "for each frame bbox, mirror the motif pixels left-to-right when the bbox is wider than tall, and top-to-bottom when it is taller than wide; preserve all existing pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16-28 rows x 16-26 cols, bg=0
  colors: exactly 2 non-bg colors; frame_color has more pixels than motif_color
  frames:
    count: 1-3 per grid, non-overlapping bboxes with >=1 cell gap
    shape: | # I-beam / bone shape, parameterized by h x w
      V (h>w): row 0 = centered 3px cap; row 1 = full-width bar with 1px center gap;
        rows 2..h-3 = left+right 1px walls; row h-2 = mirror of row 1; row h-1 = mirror of row 0
      H (w>h): transpose of V pattern (caps on left/right sides)
    dimensions:
      V frames: h 10-12 (even), w 7-11 (odd)
      H frames: h 7-9 (odd [observed]), w 10-11
    interior: region inside walls; V = (h-4) x (w-2), H = (h-2) x (w-4); 5-9 cells per side
  motif:
    pixels: 4-9 per frame
    placement: strictly in one half of interior (no pixel on or past the center axis)
    symmetry: symmetric about the perpendicular axis and centered on it
    constraint: reflected copy must not collide with frame walls (>=1 cell gap from walls)
  transform:
    rule: for each frame, reflect all motif pixels to the opposite half
    axis: H frames mirror left-right, V frames mirror top-bottom
    output = input + reflected motif pixels (bg -> motif_color)
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build symmetric output, then erase one half to get input)
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size and number of frames (1-3)
    2. For each frame, pick orientation (H or V) and dimensions per spec
    3. Place frames on grid with non-overlapping bboxes (>=1 gap)
    4. Draw the I-beam frame shape using the formula
    5. Design motif pattern inside one half of interior, ensuring perpendicular-axis
       symmetry, centered on perpendicular axis, >=1 cell from all walls
    6. Reflect motif to opposite half -> this is the output
    7. Erase the reflected half's motif pixels (set to bg) -> this is the input
